## Commands

<!-- @if uv -->
- `just install` installs the tools and the git hooks.
<!-- @else -->
- `just install` turns on the git hooks in `.githooks` and lists any tool you still need to install.
<!-- @endif -->
- `just check` runs every check that CI runs. It must pass before you finish.
- `just` lists every recipe.

## Commits and pull requests

- Commit messages and pull request titles follow
  [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `<type>[scope][!]: <description>`.
  Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `perf`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `style`,
  `revert`. The description is lowercase, in the imperative mood, with no final period.
- A pull request is squash-merged, so its title becomes the commit on `__BRANCH__`.
<!-- @if release -->
  commitizen reads that commit to choose the next version: `feat` raises the minor number, `fix`
  the patch number, and `!` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer marks a breaking change. `docs`,
  `chore`, `ci`, `build`, `test`, `style` and `refactor` do not cause a release.
<!-- @else -->
  The release tool reads that commit to choose the next version.
<!-- @endif -->
- A change to what the software does is `feat` or `fix`, even when the file is Markdown.
<!-- @if release -->
- Never edit `CHANGELOG.md` or a version number by hand. The release workflow writes both.
<!-- @endif -->

## Writing

- Write comments, documentation and commit messages in simple, direct English. Use short
  sentences. Avoid idioms. Expand each acronym the first time it appears.
- Documentation ships in the same change as the code, in `docs/` and `README.md`.
<!-- @if adr -->
- Decision records in `docs/adr/` are never edited after they are accepted. A changed
  decision is a new record that supersedes the old one.
<!-- @endif -->

## GitHub Actions

- Pin every action by full commit SHA, with the version in a comment. Dependabot keeps the
  pins current.
- Start every workflow with `permissions: {}`. Each job asks only for what it needs.
- A workflow runs `just <recipe>` instead of repeating the commands, so CI and a laptop run
  the same thing.
